-- of 1934 only through whether a class or series is "listed on a national securities exchange".
--
-- COUNTS ARE VOTES (keel fork F5): where the certificate gives more or less than one vote per share, the counts are of votes.

§ `s 251(h) -- the merger after a tender offer`

§§ `s 251(h)(6) the terms the subsection defines`

-- (h)(6)e. "Person" means any individual, corporation, partnership, limited liability company, unincorporated association or
-- other entity: every constructor of the core's Kind of entity is one of these (a natural person is an individual; a
-- statutory trust, business trust, real estate investment trust, common-law trust and any other unincorporated business are
-- "other entit[ies]"; a joint-stock association is an unincorporated association).
-- src:1105 | e. “Person” means any individual, corporation, partnership, limited liability company, unincorporated association or other entity;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(h)(6)e. (src:1105)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(h)(6)e. the kind of entity is a person` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a natural person`                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation` k                           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a general partnership`                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited partnership`                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership`           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability limited partnership`   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability company`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory trust`                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a business trust or association`           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a real estate investment trust`            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a common-law trust`                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a joint-stock association`                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other unincorporated business or association` THEN TRUE

-- (h)(6)a. "Affiliate" means, in respect of the corporation making the offer, any person that (i) owns, directly or
-- indirectly, all of the outstanding stock of that corporation, or (ii) is a direct or indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of
-- that corporation or of any person referred to in (i).
