§§ `s 251(h) the conditions, the certification and the filing`

-- The constituent corporation has "a class or series of stock that is listed on a national securities exchange or held of
-- record by more than 2,000 holders immediately prior to the execution of the agreement of merger": 2,000 holders is not
-- enough, 2,001 is.
-- src:1091 | no vote of stockholders of a constituent corporation that has a class or series of stock that is listed on a national securities exchange or held of record by more than 2,000 holders immediately prior to the execution of the agreement of merger by such constituent corporation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(h) (src:1091)
GIVEN `a class or series of its stock is listed on a national securities exchange immediately before the execution of the agreement of merger` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: federal securities law (the Securities Exchange Act of 1934)
      `the largest number of holders of record of any one class or series of its stock immediately before the execution of the agreement of merger` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(h) the constituent corporation has stock listed or held of record by more than 2,000 holders` `a class or series of its stock is listed on a national securities exchange immediately before the execution of the agreement of merger` `the largest number of holders of record of any one class or series of its stock immediately before the execution of the agreement of merger` MEANS
        `a class or series of its stock is listed on a national securities exchange immediately before the execution of the agreement of merger`
    OR `the largest number of holders of record of any one class or series of its stock immediately before the execution of the agreement of merger` GREATER THAN 2000

-- The five conditions, one field each. Condition (3) is the answer of the rule above, so it is a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
