-- All of (h)(1) to (h)(5), the corporation having the class or series described in the lead-in, and the certificate of
-- incorporation not "expressly" requiring a vote. NOTHING when condition (3) is not covered and nothing else defeats the exemption.
-- src:1091 | (h) Notwithstanding the requirements of subsection (c) of this section, unless expressly required by its certificate of incorporation, no vote of stockholders of a constituent corporation that has a class or series of stock that is listed on a national securities exchange or held of record by more than 2,000 holders immediately prior to the execution of the agreement of merger by such constituent corporation shall be necessary to authorize a merger if:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(h) (src:1091)
GIVEN `the constituent corporation has stock listed or held of record by more than 2,000 holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation of the constituent corporation expressly requires a vote of its stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      terms                                                                            IS A `s 251(h) Terms of the merger and the offer`
      `the stock held after the offer reaches the vote that would have been required for the stock and for each class or series` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(h) no vote of the stockholders of the constituent corporation is necessary` `the constituent corporation has stock listed or held of record by more than 2,000 holders` `the certificate of incorporation of the constituent corporation expressly requires a vote of its stockholders` terms `the stock held after the offer reaches the vote that would have been required for the stock and for each class or series` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `the constituent corporation has stock listed or held of record by more than 2,000 holders`
            AND (NOT `the certificate of incorporation of the constituent corporation expressly requires a vote of its stockholders`)
            AND terms's `the agreement of merger expressly permits or requires the merger to be effected under s 251(h)`
            AND terms's `the agreement of merger expressly provides that the merger shall be effected as soon as practicable following the consummation of the offer if it is effected under s 251(h)`
            AND terms's `a corporation has consummated an offer, on the terms provided in the agreement of merger, for all of the outstanding stock of the constituent corporation that, absent s 251(h), would be entitled to vote on the agreement, other than excluded stock`
            AND terms's `the corporation that consummated the offer merges with or into the constituent corporation pursuant to the agreement of merger`
            AND terms's `each outstanding share, other than excluded stock, that is the subject of the offer and was not irrevocably accepted in it is to be converted in the merger into the same amount and kind of cash, property, rights or securities as were paid for the shares of its class or series that were irrevocably accepted`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `the stock held after the offer reaches the vote that would have been required for the stock and for each class or series`

-- Certification by the secretary or assistant secretary of the surviving corporation: that the agreement was adopted under
-- (h) and that the conditions "(other than the condition listed in paragraph (h)(4))" are satisfied -- the merger of the
-- offeror into the constituent corporation has not happened yet when the certificate is made.
-- src:1108 | If an agreement of merger is adopted without the vote of stockholders of a corporation pursuant to this subsection, the secretary or assistant secretary of the surviving corporation shall certify on the agreement that the agreement has been adopted pursuant to this subsection and that the conditions specified in this subsection (other than the condition listed in paragraph (h)(4) of this section) have been satisfied; provided that such certification on the agreement shall not be required if a certificate of merger is filed in lieu of filing the agreement. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(h) (src:1108)
GIVEN `the agreement was adopted without the vote of stockholders pursuant to s 251(h)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of merger is filed in lieu of filing the agreement`                 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(h) the secretary or assistant secretary of the surviving corporation must certify that the agreement was adopted under s 251(h) and that its conditions other than (h)(4) are satisfied` `the agreement was adopted without the vote of stockholders pursuant to s 251(h)` `a certificate of merger is filed in lieu of filing the agreement` MEANS
        `the agreement was adopted without the vote of stockholders pursuant to s 251(h)`
    AND (NOT `a certificate of merger is filed in lieu of filing the agreement`)

-- src:1108 | The agreement so adopted and certified shall then be filed and shall become effective, in accordance with § 103 of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(h) (src:1108)
GIVEN `the agreement has been adopted under s 251(h) and certified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(h) the agreement so adopted and certified is then to be filed` `the agreement has been adopted under s 251(h) and certified` MEANS
    `the agreement has been adopted under s 251(h) and certified`

-- src:1108 | Such filing shall constitute a representation by the person who executes the agreement that the facts stated in the certificate remain true immediately prior to such filing.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(h) (src:1108)
GIVEN `the agreement adopted under s 251(h) and certified is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(h) the person who executes the agreement represents that the facts stated in the certificate remain true` `the agreement adopted under s 251(h) and certified is filed` MEANS
    `the agreement adopted under s 251(h) and certified is filed`
